   "ruling": "Ruling: scope; project retained, as ruled on this line in earlier rounds (s1a render sidecar, the same objection). Schedule 1-A line 36b: \"If you are married filing jointly, your spouse has a valid social security number (see instructions), and your spouse was born before January 2, 1961, enter the amount from line 35\"; i1040gi p. 110: \"If you are married, you must file a joint return with your spouse to claim this deduction.\" A spouse entry exists only on a joint return: household.roster_ok requires one spouse entry exactly when filing jointly, and any other roster is refused at Form 1040 line 1a (household.roster_bad; Form 1040 page 1, \"If joint return, spouse's first name\"). The spouse count now reads person.spouse_senior_work_ssn (role, then age, then SSN, in that order), the same conjunction, so the restatement is unchanged and so is the reading.",
